      { "text": "Hirschsprung disease.", "explanation": "Incorrect. Hirschsprung is a congenital disorder presenting in infancy/childhood with megacolon and constipation, not in older adults with multi-system features. This would be the correct answer if the patient were a newborn with delayed meconium passage." },
      { "text": "Dressler syndrome (post-MI pericardial inflammation).", "explanation": "Incorrect. Dressler syndrome is a post-MI inflammatory pericarditis, not the multi-system Chagas triad. This would be the correct answer if the patient had a recent MI with new pleuritic chest pain and pericardial effusion." }
